WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.226 --> 00:00:01.459
- Can I ask a question?

00:00:01.459 --> 00:00:02.292
- Um hmm.

00:00:02.292 --> 00:00:03.517
- If you can't get these
across state lines,

00:00:03.517 --> 00:00:05.017
how did you do it?

00:00:05.958 --> 00:00:07.442
- (laughs)

00:00:07.442 --> 00:00:10.453
(upbeat music)

00:00:10.453 --> 00:00:12.402
- I took a quick road trip
from New York to Montreal

00:00:12.402 --> 00:00:14.873
this weekend in the pouring rain.

00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:16.407
I brought back a few items that you just

00:00:16.407 --> 00:00:20.238
can't find stateside, just
so my coworkers can try 'em.

00:00:20.238 --> 00:00:22.030
They better like 'em.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.613
- [Group] Surprise!

00:00:25.508 --> 00:00:26.341
- Yes.

00:00:27.201 --> 00:00:28.678
- Oh!
- Yes!

00:00:28.678 --> 00:00:30.737
These are like legit banned.

00:00:30.737 --> 00:00:31.620
- Kendra's surprised.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.635
- Not for resale in the
United States. Damn!

00:00:34.635 --> 00:00:36.087
- Here you go.

00:00:36.087 --> 00:00:38.553
- Is there gonna be a
prize when we open it up?

00:00:38.553 --> 00:00:39.608
- Am I gonna choke on camera?

00:00:39.608 --> 00:00:42.163
- Offhand, I don't know
what this is about.

00:00:42.163 --> 00:00:43.069
- Ooo.

00:00:43.069 --> 00:00:43.902
- Mmm.

00:00:43.902 --> 00:00:47.699
- So, I don't understand how
people are getting injured

00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:50.402
when it's literally in another egg.

00:00:50.402 --> 00:00:51.625
- I'm trying to go for a child's bite.

00:00:51.625 --> 00:00:53.788
- Do it. Ready. Go.

00:00:53.788 --> 00:00:54.621
- (mumbles)

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:55.454
- Oh.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:56.311
- Oh.

00:00:56.311 --> 00:01:00.109
- I bit the thing and I
couldn't bite any farther.

00:01:00.109 --> 00:01:02.351
There was no more biting.
Oh my gosh, there's like

00:01:02.351 --> 00:01:03.359
things. What?

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:04.192
- Yeah.

00:01:04.192 --> 00:01:05.287
- I thought it was just a
toy. There's like accessories?

00:01:05.287 --> 00:01:06.598
- The toy is not the egg.

00:01:06.598 --> 00:01:08.176
- What is this, ChapStick inside?

00:01:08.176 --> 00:01:11.551
That would be nice, though.
You eat it, and then you

00:01:11.551 --> 00:01:13.625
"oh, my lip's a little chapped."

00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:15.966
- We have plenty of toys
like this in America

00:01:15.966 --> 00:01:17.288
that kids choke on.

00:01:17.288 --> 00:01:19.362
- Well I just think because
it's coming in the chocolate,

00:01:19.362 --> 00:01:20.391
they're like this whole thing--

00:01:20.391 --> 00:01:21.269
- Is edible.

00:01:21.269 --> 00:01:23.165
- Must be something that
I can eat right now.

00:01:23.165 --> 00:01:25.861
- Do Canadian kids not choke on plastic

00:01:25.861 --> 00:01:27.251
and choke on these things?

00:01:27.251 --> 00:01:29.231
Why can they have it and we can't?

00:01:29.231 --> 00:01:31.932
- I think Canadian kids
just might be smarter.

00:01:31.932 --> 00:01:33.076
In the long run.

00:01:33.076 --> 00:01:35.659
(upbeat music)

00:01:39.455 --> 00:01:41.461
- Oh, it's a shot!

00:01:41.461 --> 00:01:42.783
- We're getting drunk.

00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:43.854
- Ooo!

00:01:43.854 --> 00:01:46.498
- It smells like, oh my God, is this...

00:01:46.498 --> 00:01:47.814
- It smells like licorice.

00:01:47.814 --> 00:01:49.716
- This is Absinthe.
- Oh God.

00:01:49.716 --> 00:01:53.549
- Are you trying to make
us black out at work?

00:01:55.528 --> 00:01:57.195
- Oh. Okay.
- Oh. Ew.

00:01:58.757 --> 00:02:00.607
- Woo! It's like, oh my God!

00:02:00.607 --> 00:02:01.440
- Ooo.

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:03.684
- (coughs)

00:02:03.684 --> 00:02:08.045
- It tastes like fireball at
first, and then it just goes

00:02:08.045 --> 00:02:12.212
to straight burning. And then
it goes back to Jager Bomb.

00:02:13.071 --> 00:02:14.628
- Please drink with extreme caution.

00:02:14.628 --> 00:02:16.440
- Isn't this the stuff that

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.901
Shakespeare used to get sauced
on, or something like that?

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:20.897
- I'm okay with that being banned.

00:02:20.897 --> 00:02:22.328
- Don't bring this shit over here.

00:02:22.328 --> 00:02:25.328
Keep this shit in Ontario. Montreal.

00:02:26.377 --> 00:02:27.516
I don't need this shit.

00:02:27.516 --> 00:02:31.158
- Canada is known universally
as the nicest country,

00:02:31.158 --> 00:02:33.859
so why would there be
things that Canada allows

00:02:33.859 --> 00:02:35.672
that other places don't allow?

00:02:35.672 --> 00:02:38.237
Free healthcare. I don't know, Absinthe.

00:02:38.237 --> 00:02:40.792
- I think Canada is trying
to give us a little time out.

00:02:40.792 --> 00:02:44.444
They're like, look, you're
wilding down there, down South.

00:02:44.444 --> 00:02:48.033
So we got these good things
over here. You can't get none.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:52.200
Sorry. But that's what happens
when you're in time out.

00:02:53.038 --> 00:02:55.621
(upbeat music)

00:02:58.860 --> 00:02:59.693
- Wow.

